# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What does not belong in the repo.
#
# The rule of thumb: anything that is downloaded, built, generated by a run, or
# specific to one machine stays out. What is left is the source, the docs and
# the recipes needed to reproduce the rest.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Model weights. 100+ GB, fetched on first start from the repo named in .env.
models/

# The Python environment start.bat builds, and anything compiled into it.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

# Locally built wheels (the README explains how to make them again).
wheels/*
!wheels/README.md

# Vendored third-party applications - a 300 MB portable .exe is not source.
apps/

# Runtime state: logs and marker files.
logs/
.simplex/

# DSH_HOME for the harness the launcher starts: its generated settings, its
# credential store, its profiles and the plugins it installs into them. The
# route in .dsh/settings.yaml is regenerated from the running server, so
# nothing in here is worth tracking - and the credential store must not be.
.dsh/

# Machine-specific configuration. .env.example is the template that IS
# tracked; .env itself holds this box's paths, ports and GPU sizes.
.env

# Working notes, not documentation. The README is what a stranger reads; this
# is a running log with dated sections and half of it about a UI that moved
# out. It stays on the machine it was written on.
HANDOFF.md

# Made by a maintainer to get back to a new-user state. It deletes the weights,
# the venv and the shortcuts, so it is not something to hand a stranger.
reset_new_user.bat

# Staging for deletion, and scratch that is nobody else's business.
_to_delete/
Claude outputs/

# Scratch a release must not sweep up. Every one of these was sitting in the
# tree untracked and unignored, which is one `git add -A` away from being
# published: a reset backup carries saved conversations, and a bundle carries
# a branch nobody asked for.
_reset_backup_*/
.reset_backup_name
_repo_for_tests.tgz
_e2e_win/
_e2e_win.tgz
*.bundle
_shot_*.png

# OS and editor droppings.
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Defensive rules. Nothing below has ever appeared in this tree; they are here
# so that a stray file from a tool nobody has run yet cannot be swept up by a
# `git add -A` on the day of a release.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Any other .env flavour a machine grows (.env.local, .env.bak, .env.spark).
# The template stays tracked.
.env.*
!.env.example

# Written by the harness config step; machine state, like .env.
providers.json

# A log written anywhere but logs/.
*.log

# npx puts its tree under .dsh/, but its cache location is not a promise.
node_modules/

# Python test and lint caches.
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Build output, if anything is ever built here.
dist/
build/

# Windows shortcuts. shortcuts.py writes these to the Start Menu and Desktop,
# not here, but a hand-made one in the tree should not be committed.
*.lnk

# Weights, in case MODEL_DIR is ever pointed somewhere other than models/.
*.safetensors
*.gguf
*.part

# Promo renders and their music. Made here, kept here - 85 MB of video and
# audio that nobody cloning the kit needs, and that every future clone would
# have to carry. The .png is the same story at a smaller size.
/*.mp4
/*.mp3
/*.png
